description.narrative:
The overall objectives of the intervention are to generate new knowledge, strengthen research capacity and promote transdisciplinary research to find solutions to global challenges.

We fund transdisciplinary research within the sustainability area through the Belmont Forum. This is done in the form of Collaborative Research Actions (CRAs) where we join forces with other funders to fund international research groups. These research groups should consist of researchers from at least three different countries where the researchers (in most cases) apply for funding from their own national research council.   

For the administration and management of funds to African research partners selected through Belmont Forum CRA calls, Sida partners with the National Research Foundation (NRF).

The agreement with NRF currently covers two different initiatives and the plan is to expand the collaboration as new calls are added to the portfolio. Currently this contribution covers a call on ocean sustainability through Belmont Forum and a call to support research related to the Covid-19 pandemic on the African continent. A call of Migration and Mobility is being added. 

The specific objectives of the Ocean Sustainability programme are:

to administer CRA grants in Somalia, Kenya, Mozambique and Madagascar;

to provide technical assistance to selected institutions to support the design, implementation and monitoring of innovative approaches and interventions for the CRA project;

to manage capacity building or networking activities to support effective delivery of the CRA programs;

to follow up on projects and reporting;

to document, process and develop a learning model capable of facilitating continuous learning, increased impact and sustainability of the funded CRA projects.



The specific objectives of the Covid-19 Africa Rapid Grant Fund are: 

to contribute to the African regional and continental response to the COVID-19 pandemic;

to support knowledge generation and translation to inform diagnostics, prevention and treatment of COVID-19 on the continent;

to Strengthen African regional and continental science engagement efforts in response to the COVID-19 pandemic; and 

to leverage existing, strong multilateral collaborations in support of Africas consolidated response to the COVID-19 pandemic and attract new collaborations from international partners.
